validity, accuracy, or non-infringement. Creative Commons recommends
that you consult with an attorney and counsel for legal advice.

Creative Commons is the originator of the Creative Commons public
licenses. Creative Commons licenses are a set of standardized public
licenses that allow individuals and organizations to share creative
works of authorship ("Works") under common, understandable, and
clearly stated terms and conditions. These licenses provide a
flexible framework to release Works for nonprofit, informational and
educational purposes while preserving moral rights and honoring the
rights of the original author and creator.

Creative Commons public licenses provide a clear and consistent
framework to release creative Works to the public.

Creative Commons public licenses are freely available for use,
modification, and redistribution.

